# OI WebUI Changelog

## 2026-04-05 — Terminal output pipeline fix + execution mode toggle

### Terminal output pipeline (critical fix)

Commands executed through OI chat were producing garbled, missing, or
duplicated output. Five root causes identified and fixed:

1. _filter_console was too aggressive — after pyte (virtual terminal
   emulator) had already processed ANSI codes and rendered clean text,
   the filter was dropping blank lines, whitespace-only content, and
   lines after \r handling. Legitimate command output silently discarded.
   Now only strips hub-specific braille spinner frames.

2. snapshot chunks treated as appends — when pyte detects screen rewrites
   (progress bars, \r overwrites), it sends {snapshot: true} meaning
   "replace previous content." The bridge ignored this flag and the client
   appended, causing duplicated/garbled output. Now the flag passes through
   and the client replaces the buffer on snapshot events.

3. active_line chunks leaking — OI sends {format: "active_line"} chunks
   for tracking code execution progress. These passed through the
   role/type check and were treated as output. Now explicitly skipped.

4. Terminal width 80 in headless mode — os.get_terminal_size() fails when
   running as a web server, falling back to 80 columns. Commands formatting
   for wider terminals got mangled by pyte line wrapping. Now defaults to
   120 columns (configurable via OI_COLUMNS env var).

### ANSI colors in chat output (fix)

Colored command output in chat appeared as unstyled white text. ANSI color
CSS classes (.ansi-green, .ansi-red, etc.) were scoped to .terminal-block
and .magic-output-body only — chat output uses .console-output which had
no rules. Removed scoping; ANSI classes are now global. Added missing
styles: ansi-black, ansi-italic, ansi-underline, ansi-strikethrough, plus
their SGR codes in both server-side and client-side parsers.

### Execution mode toggle (new feature)

Three-mode toggle above the chat input:

  Ask   — Confirms every command before running
  Safe  — Auto-runs safe commands (ls, cat, grep, hub tools...),
          confirms unsafe ones (rm, sudo, pip...) [default]
  Auto  — Runs everything without confirmation

Persisted in config.json, survives restarts. Synced from server on load.

### Files modified

  oi_bridge.py                  Snapshot passthrough, filter rewrite,
                                active_line skip, exec_mode logic
  server.py                     POST /api/session/exec-mode endpoint,
                                expanded SGR map
  static/js/chat.js             Snapshot replace, exec mode UI,
                                expanded client SGR map
  static/js/webui.js            Sync exec_mode from session on load
  static/index.html             Exec mode toggle markup
  static/css/shared.css         Global ANSI classes, new styles
  static/css/webui.css          Exec mode toggle styling
  interpreter/.../              Terminal width fallback 80 -> 120
    subprocess_language.py
